  "report_period": "Week 14 (28th Mar to 4th Apr 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Capesize \"Arabella\" 177/2005 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 02/2028, DD 02/2026, Scrubber fitted) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 18 mill. Note that a couple of months ago, the \"Cape Friendship\" 185/2005 Kawasaki, Japan (SS 03/2027, DD 06/2025) was sold at USD 16,1 mill. Following the sale of the Post Panamax \"Cora Oldendorff\" 93/2012 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 04/2025, Scrubber fitted) back in February at USD 13,8 mill, Oldendorff Carriers have now sold the \"Clemens Oldendorff\" 92/2012 Cosco, China (SS 01/2027, DD 05/2025) at USD 13,3 mill. The Kamsarmax \"Sea Marathon\" 81/2015 Qingdao, China (SS/DD 09/2025) was committed to Greek interests at USD 18,4 mill. Remind you that back in December, the one-year-older \"Hellenic C\" 81/2014 Jiangsu, China (SS 09/2029, DD 10/2027) was sold at USD 21 mill. Hellenic Star Shipping committed their Panamax \"Sea Charm\" 75/2003 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 04/2026) to Chinese interests at USD 7,7 mill. For comparison, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Anais\" 76/2002 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 02/2027, DD 05/2025) was sold back in January at USD 5,6 mill. On the Supramax sector, Virono Shipping committed their \"Volissos\" 57/2010 Qingshan, China (SS/DD 07/2025) to Chinese interests at USD 10,7 mill, while the \"SFL Yukon\" 56/2010 Xiamen, China (SS/DD 12/2025) was committed to Chinese interests also at USD 10,2 mill. Note that back in January, the \"Protector St. Raphael\" 56/2010 Xiamen, China (SS/DD 07/2025) was sold at USD 11 mill. In addition, NVL Trans Shipping committed their \"Mercurius\" 50/2001 Mitsui, Japan (SS 01/2026, DD 09/2025) at high USD 5 mill, while the sister vessel \"Sirina\" 50/2001 Mitsui, Japan (SS 11/2027, DD 11/2025) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 6,85 mill. The Handysize \"Queen Harmony\" 28/2011 I-S, Japan (SS/DD 03/2026) was committed to undisclosed interests at low USD 10 mill. Remind you that the sister vessel \"Woodgate\" 28/2011 I-S, Japan (SS/DD 05/2026) was sold in January at USD 10,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "MJL Bangladesh have committed their Aframax \"Omera Legacy\" 107/2005 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 05/2025) at region USD 25 mill. Note that back in February, the two-years-older \"Sea Luck III\" 105/2003 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS 07/2028, DD 10/2026) was sold at USD 25 mill. The MR1 \"SW Cap Ferrat I\" 36/2002 Stx, Korea (SS 03/2027, DD 07/2025) of Sea World Management SAM was committed to Chinese interests at high USD 7 mill. For comparison, the \"Yash\" 37/2002 Stx, Korea (SS 05/2027, DD 08/2025) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 8,2 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout round trips on the same route were reported around usd 22,000/23,000 pd levels. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 14,000/16,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 13,000/16,000 pd. Indonesian and Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 14,000/17,000 pd. Continental trips via North Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 17,000/19,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/700K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 14,850 pd for 4/6 months employment basis delivery China. Also, a Kamsarmax was fixed on a period at the usd 15,500 pd basis delivery China for 1 year employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed at the level of usd 9,000/12,000 pd. Indian trips into China were fixed around usd 6,000/8,000 pd. South American trips into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into West Coast South America were fixed around usd 17,000/18,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from Caribbean into Continent were reported at the level of usd 7,000/9,000 pd. South American trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 14,000/15,000 pd. Also trips from South America into West Africa were reported at the level of usd 12,000/13,000 pd. South American trips into Far East were fixed around usd 13,000/14,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
